{
 "about": "The cases common to every pairing's read, the public half of the read kit, for the profile read-status (lcp/profiles/read-status.md). Each case states what a read observed, in the profile's own terms: the transactions it met, each with its position, the mark it was read at, its result, whether it consumed the act's single-use value, whether it carries H, its signer against the payer and the option's payee, its pairing and kind, and the account it names; the single-use value as read, absent where the read has no means to read it; whether the search or lookup was read whole, and its position where it was not; and whether the reader showed its history. Positions are integers; marks are 'included', 'safe' and 'final', in that order. Each expected answer was derived by hand from the rules of read-status.md the case names, for the act 'payment' and for the act 'agreement', and none was taken from the package's output. An expected answer lists the members the answer must hold; foreign items are listed with their transaction and reason. A pairing's own vectors run each case through its reader, mapping each transaction and position to its ledger's, or state that the case cannot arise on its ledger.",
 "marks": [
  "included",
  "safe",
  "final"
 ],
 "cases": [
  {
